# prohibit-tags — a kind prohibited only when carrying a declared taint tag.
# `deploy` is prohibited when the token is tagged `untrusted_model`. Two gates share
# the one prohibition: the tagged token at g1 is severed (prohibited -> withhold),
# while an otherwise-identical untagged deploy at g2 is unprohibited and releasable
# (auto -> act). A guarded prohibition prohibits exactly the matched subset (SPEC §6);
# membership over a declared category, not branching on identity.
actor a
gate g1 risk high grant a
gate g2 risk high grant a
prohibit deploy when tags contains untrusted_model
cord a -> g1
cord a -> g2
cord g1 -> master
cord g2 -> master
